      "message": "I was a little surprised at the gold diffs, but they are all from Radeon GPUs. I looked at a frame capture on my M1 and all of the intermediates are exact-fit HW textures. However, a lot of them use the DontCare/Discard load op and we have the issue with coverage+src rendering right now thinking it needs to blend with the dst.\n\nMy current theory is that the src-blend w/ dst readback and what should amount to 100% coverage is not quite a perfect src-blend on Radeon so we see some discarded/random values leaking through slightly. This should be fixed when the proper non-aa blit is added.",
